Additional permission under GNU GPL version 3 section 7 — SDR hardware APIs
---------------------------------------------------------------------------

SignalScribe talks to receiver hardware through vendor-supplied APIs that are
not free software. The SDRplay API (sdrplay_api) is proprietary, is distributed
by SDRplay Ltd. under its own terms, and cannot be relicensed by this project.
Without an explicit permission, distributing a GPLv3 binary linked against it
would be legally awkward, which would make the program undistributable in the
only form in which it is useful.

Therefore, as a special exception, the copyright holder of SignalScribe gives
you permission to link this program with, and to convey the resulting work
under the GPL, code that interfaces with proprietary SDR hardware support
libraries, specifically including but not limited to the SDRplay API
(sdrplay_api), and to copy and distribute the resulting executable under terms
of your choice for the linking portion, provided that you also meet the terms
and conditions of the GNU General Public License for every other part of the
work.

If you modify this program, you may extend this exception to your version of
the program, but you are not obliged to do so. If you do not wish to do so,
delete this exception statement from your version.


